What:		/dev/pwm-wave-N
Date:		July 2026
KernelVersion:	6.1
Contact:	Rockchip Linux <linux@rock-chips.com>
Description:
		A character-device interface to a Rockchip PWM v4 wave-table
		generator.

		PWM_WAVE_IOC_GET_CAPS reports the ABI version and lookup-table
		capacities. PWM_WAVE_IOC_SET_CONFIG sets the fixed PWM period,
		requested wave clock, per-entry repeat value and lookup-table
		width.

		A write submits one complete duty lookup table and starts the
		wave generator from entry zero. The write buffer is an array of
		native-endian __u32 duty durations in nanoseconds. Each duration
		must not exceed the configured period. The complete array must
		fit the selected 8-bit or 16-bit hardware table.

		PWM_WAVE_IOC_STOP stops the output and leaves it at its inactive
		polarity. Closing the descriptor does not stop a running wave.

		Protocol interpretation belongs to userspace. For example,
		WS2812 and SK6812 clients encode their bits and reset interval as
		duty-duration entries before write().
